│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ demand_aware_path_synergy                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Keep the baseline reward for direct demand, and add two restrained quadratic signals: a   │
│                          │ small reward when two selected links form a two-hop route for a demanded OD pair, and a   │
│                          │ reciprocal-link reward proportional to the weaker of the two directional demands. The     │
│                          │ two-hop coefficient is deliberately modest so that merely creating path motifs does not   │
│                          │ dominate direct-link value, as happened with the naive larger reward. Both signals use    │
│                          │ only demand data, and the number of terms is O(n³), within the limit. The degree penalty  │
│                          │ remains external, so its weight is unchanged.                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
