╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ weaken_noisy_transit_rewards                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program’s two-hop rewards can make the annealer favor routes through a node   │
│                          │ simply because they create a short path, even when that node is already busy or the route │
│                          │ is not useful for balancing link loads. The current congestion discount helps, but the    │
│                          │ measured median gap is still worse than with the earlier, undiscouted two-hop model.      │
