│ patch_description        │ This approach combines direct-demand rewards with an endpoint-access signal: a link is    │
│                          │ valuable when its source generates traffic and its destination attracts traffic. Unlike   │
│                          │ rewarding individual two-hop paths, it adds positive quadratic penalties for selecting    │
│                          │ links that serve highly similar demand profiles from the same source or into the same     │
│                          │ destination. With degree two, this encourages each node’s two links to provide            │
│                          │ complementary access rather than redundant access, while keeping the quadratic term count │
│                          │ within the limit.                                                                         │
