│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ neighbor_role_diversity                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Keep the baseline direct-demand reward, and add a modest positive interaction for         │
│                          │ selecting links whose endpoints have similar network roles. Two outgoing neighbors with   │
│                          │ similar demand profiles offer redundant downstream options; likewise, two incoming        │
│                          │ neighbors with similar profiles offer redundant origins. Penalizing these pairs           │
│                          │ encourages the two links at each node to provide more diverse routing options, while the  │
│                          │ direct-demand reward still favors useful links. Cosine normalization makes the            │
│                          │ interactions comparable across nodes with different total demand. The construction adds   │
│                          │ at most \(n(n-1)(n-2)\) quadratic terms.                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
