│ patch_name               │ max_pressure_path_cover                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This combines the direct-demand signal with a second-order path-coverage reward: a pair   │
│                          │ of selected links earns credit for carrying traffic that could otherwise require a direct │
│                          │ link. To avoid giving every possible two-hop route the full value of the same demand, the │
│                          │ path reward is shared across the four routes an OD pair could use under degree-two        │
│                          │ constraints.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The novel calibration uses maximum-normalized incident traffic to discount busy transit   │
│                          │ nodes, with a bounded inverse pressure factor. It also discounts routes whose component   │
│                          │ links already have substantial direct demand, since those links may have less spare       │
│                          │ capacity. A small endpoint-throughput contribution in the linear terms preserves useful   │
│                          │ source and destination signals without displacing direct demand.                          │
