│ patch_name               │ pressure_gated_paths                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This design keeps direct-demand rewards, but uses a distinct pressure-gated two-hop       │
│                          │ signal: a path is considered only when its origin–destination pair has positive demand,   │
│                          │ and its reward is reduced when the transit node is busy or either path edge already has   │
│                          │ substantial direct demand. Unlike uniform allocation across possible intermediates, it    │
│                          │ does not divide an OD pair’s reward among all candidate paths; instead, each candidate    │
│                          │ path receives a modest reward, allowing useful alternatives to remain visible to the      │
│                          │ sampler. The total quadratic-term count is bounded by the number of eligible two-hop      │
│                          │ paths, at most n(n−1)(n−2).                                                               │
