│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ endpoint_congestion_paths                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This design keeps the direct-demand signal simple, but adds a different kind of quadratic │
│                          │ term: a congestion proxy for pairs of selected links that both leave the same node or     │
│                          │ both enter the same node. Such pairs are especially undesirable when their direct traffic │
│                          │ is already substantial and the shared endpoint has high incident demand. To avoid         │
│                          │ rewarding every possible two-hop route equally, it adds small, pressure-discounted        │
│                          │ rewards only for the two most plausible intermediate nodes per OD pair. This combines     │
│                          │ endpoint load balancing with a deliberately sparse path signal, staying within the        │
│                          │ quadratic-term limit.                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
