│ patch_description        │ Replace mean-based transit-node pressure with each node’s larger incoming or outgoing     │
│                          │ demand, normalized by the largest such value across nodes. This makes the discount        │
│                          │ respond to the busiest incident direction rather than an average that can hide a heavily  │
│                          │ loaded node. Keep the existing two-hop reward formula unchanged and use a 0.75 floor:     │
│                          │ even the busiest node remains a plausible transit point, while less-loaded nodes receive  │
│                          │ a modestly larger share of indirect-route reward.                                         │
