│ patch_description        │ This version keeps direct demand as the strongest link signal and adds a modest concave   │
│                          │ term so medium-demand direct links remain visible. Two-hop incentives are capped          │
│                          │ separately for each origin–destination pair: all candidate intermediates together receive │
│                          │ at most a fixed fraction of that pair’s normalized demand, rather than accumulating an    │
│                          │ incentive proportional to the number of intermediates. The cap is allocated using         │
│                          │ component-link support and a mild transit-load discount, with a uniform share mixed in to │
│                          │ preserve alternatives. Input demands are sanitized, and the degree penalty is             │
│                          │ strengthened slightly to encourage feasible samples.                                      │
