│                          │ demand / scale`. The current per-intermediate reward is divided by four, reflecting the   │
│                          │ maximum number of such paths in a valid degree-two topology, but summing over all         │
│                          │ candidate intermediates can exceed that budget. Rescale an OD pair’s existing candidate   │
│                          │ rewards only when their sum exceeds the cap. This retains the current transit preference  │
│                          │ and supported-path structure while preventing many possible intermediates from            │
│                          │ collectively overwhelming the direct-link signal; it does not add quadratic terms.        │
