                        Patch Metadata - Gen 82/200 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_aware_paths                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Discount each two-hop candidate when either component link already has high direct        │
│                          │ demand. Those links are plausible routes, but rewarding them as transit links as well may │
│                          │ concentrate load and worsen the maximum-link objective. A mild, symmetric congestion      │
│                          │ factor keeps the existing support and transit-node preferences while steering some        │
│                          │ indirect reward toward less-loaded components. This changes only the allocation among     │
