│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ capped_detour_support                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The earlier programs reward every possible two-hop route independently, so the total      │
│                          │ reward for one OD pair can grow with the number of candidate transit nodes and overwhelm  │
│                          │ the direct-link signal. This design instead treats detours as a limited backup budget:    │
│                          │ for each OD pair, it scores candidate intermediates by transit-node pressure and existing │
│                          │ demand on the route edges, then distributes a capped total reward across them. Direct     │
│                          │ demand remains the main signal, while selective detours can still influence which links   │
│                          │ are chosen. The number of quadratic terms remains within the required bound.              │
