│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ clamped_route_quality                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current two-hop reward applies across every possible intermediate node, so routes     │
│                          │ through relatively poor transit points can still receive substantial reward. This edit    │
│                          │ computes a quality for each candidate route from the existing transit-node and            │
│                          │ edge-pressure signals, normalizes those qualities to their per-OD mean, and clamps their  │
│                          │ relative influence to 0.8–1.4. The clamp limits how much any single route can dominate    │
│                          │ while still preferring better-supported, less-congested alternatives. The existing route  │
│                          │ reward, direct-link terms, and degree-penalty setting remain unchanged.                   │
