│ patch_description        │ This approach builds a congestion-aware menu of two-hop routes. For each                  │
│                          │ origin-destination pair, it distributes a bounded routing reward across candidate relays, │
│                          │ favoring relays and constituent links with lower estimated traffic pressure. Direct links │
│                          │ retain a separate service reward. Unlike a uniform two-hop bonus, the route rewards       │
│                          │ compete for a fixed per-pair budget, so adding more candidate paths does not inflate      │
│                          │ their total influence. The construction uses at most \(n(n-1)(n-2)\) quadratic terms.     │
