│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ congestion_aware_relay                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This design keeps direct-demand rewards but changes the two-hop signal to favor routes    │
│                          │ through relays and links with more estimated spare capacity. Relay pressure blends        │
│                          │ mean-normalized and max-normalized estimates, with a floor so a busy node is discouraged  │
│                          │ rather than ruled out. Candidate paths are ranked using both relay pressure and the       │
│                          │ direct-demand burden on their component links; a capped reward is then shared among the   │
│                          │ best candidates for each OD pair. This combines the earlier programs’ direct-service and  │
│                          │ two-hop ideas while making route selection explicitly congestion-aware.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
