│ patch_description        │ Raise the two-hop reward strength from 0.25 to 0.46. The current surrogate already        │
│                          │ rewards only positive-demand two-hop routes and discounts pressured intermediates, but    │
│                          │ its route reward may be too weak to influence topology selection relative to direct-link  │
│                          │ rewards. This targeted increase follows the suggested strength sweep while staying below  │
│                          │ 0.56, which may help sampled topologies serve more traffic through useful routes without  │
│                          │ making the two-hop terms dominant. It does not change the term count or degree-penalty    │
│                          │ handling.                                                                                 │
