│ patch_description        │ Keep the route-quality, congestion, and indirect-budget settings unchanged, but apply a   │
│                          │ 0.75 floor to the existing max-normalized relay pressure. This isolates the effect of     │
│                          │ pressure normalization: very quiet nodes no longer receive a disproportionate transit     │
│                          │ reward solely because their incident demand is small, while busier nodes retain their     │
│                          │ relative pressure. The floor is a focused test of the suggested max-based normalization   │
│                          │ variants and avoids changing unrelated route-scoring behavior.                            │
