│                          │ scoring. Instead of spreading each OD pair’s indirect reward across every possible        │
│                          │ intermediate, it retains only its three strongest supported two-hop routes, with          │
│                          │ congestion discounting based on component-edge demand and transit-node pressure. This     │
│                          │ reduces quadratic-term count, avoids rewarding implausible routes, and keeps the indirect │
│                          │ reward budget bounded per OD pair. The returned interface and evaluator-supplied degree   │
│                          │ penalties are unchanged.                                                                  │
