│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ narrow_path_quality                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current concave path support gives smaller OD demands substantially more relative     │
│                          │ influence than large demands. Narrow that variation by applying a bounded multiplier to   │
│                          │ each path’s existing support: clamp its ratio to normalized demand to [0.8, 1.4]. This    │
│                          │ preserves the current path-strength and transit-pressure terms while limiting how much    │
│                          │ concavity can distort the relative importance of OD pairs. For normalized demand in (0,   │
│                          │ 1], this mainly caps the boost given to small demands; the lower bound keeps the          │
│                          │ formulation well-defined if the demand model is later adjusted.                           │
