│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cap_two_hop_support                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current two-hop terms can accumulate across all \(n-2\) intermediate nodes for each   │
│                          │ OD pair, so their combined influence may greatly exceed that pair’s direct-link reward.   │
│                          │ Keep the existing path-quality ranking, but rescale the terms for each OD pair together   │
│                          │ when their total magnitude exceeds 50% of its linear reward. This limits aggregate        │
│                          │ two-hop influence without changing which intermediate paths are preferred, and leaves OD  │
│                          │ pairs with no direct demand without two-hop rewards.                                      │
