│ patch_name               │ balanced_twohop                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This hybrid keeps the current implementation’s concave demand component, so               │
│                          │ moderate-demand direct links and paths still matter, while shifting both signals toward   │
│                          │ the inspiration program’s direct-demand weighting. It also adopts the inspiration’s       │
│                          │ stronger discount for paths whose component links already carry direct traffic.           │
│                          │ Transit-node pressure discourages reliance on busy intermediate nodes, and a slightly     │
│                          │ stronger degree penalty is intended to keep annealing samples closer to valid topologies. │
│                          │ Quadratic terms are generated only for positive-demand OD pairs, so the term count stays  │
│                          │ below \(n^3\).                                                                            │
