│ patch_name               │ mean_pressure_floor                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Normalize relay pressure by mean incident demand rather than the maximum, with a 0.75     │
│                          │ floor. Maximum-based normalization compresses pressure differences because the busiest    │
│                          │ node is fixed at 1 while many other nodes hit the floor. Mean normalization makes the     │
│                          │ discount reflect how busy a relay is relative to the network overall; the higher floor    │
│                          │ limits excessive preference for quiet nodes. This changes only the route discount,        │
│                          │ leaving the existing path-quality formula and term count intact.                          │
