│ patch_name               │ sparse-relay-balance                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses max-normalized relay pressure and spreads every two-hop reward   │
│                          │ across all possible intermediates. This version uses mean-normalized pressure with a      │
│                          │ higher 0.85 floor, then allocates each OD pair’s indirect reward to at most four          │
│                          │ promising relays. It adds a modest penalty for redundant incoming or outgoing neighbor    │
│                          │ profiles, while keeping the total number of quadratic terms well below the allowed limit. │
│                          │ The direct-link reward remains demand-focused, with a smaller endpoint contribution.      │
