│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cap_aggregate_twohop                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current quadratic reward is assigned independently for every eligible intermediate    │
│                          │ node. As n grows, the aggregate reward for routing one OD pair indirectly can therefore   │
│                          │ become much larger than the reward for its direct link, biasing the QUBO toward path      │
│                          │ support rather than useful direct connections. Keep the existing transit-pressure         │
│                          │ preferences, but scale all candidate two-hop rewards for each OD pair together so their   │
│                          │ total magnitude is at most 65% of that pair’s direct-link reward. This preserves relative │
│                          │ preferences between intermediates while limiting indirect terms’ influence on both the    │
│                          │ best and typical sampled topologies.                                                      │
