├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cap_indirect_support                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current two-hop reward for an OD pair is repeated across every possible intermediate  │
│                          │ node. Even with pressure discounts, its aggregate can therefore outweigh the reward for   │
│                          │ serving that OD pair directly, making indirect routes too influential in the low-energy   │
│                          │ region. Keep the existing route-quality estimates, but rescale each OD pair’s two-hop     │
│                          │ terms together so their total absolute reward is at most 60% of that pair’s direct-link   │
│                          │ reward. This preserves preferences among candidate relays while limiting the incentive to │
│                          │ accumulate many indirect-route terms; it should help prevent indirect rewards from        │
│                          │ distorting both the best and typical sampled topologies.                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0012                                                                                   │
