│ patch_name               │ fractional_route_balance                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of rewarding every two-hop path independently, this approach estimates how much   │
│                          │ each possible link would carry under a demand-weighted fractional routing model. Direct   │
│                          │ paths receive priority; remaining traffic is distributed over two-hop alternatives,       │
│                          │ discounted when they use busy intermediate nodes. The resulting estimated link loads      │
│                          │ define linear congestion costs, while quadratic terms penalize pairs of links that would  │
│                          │ jointly concentrate load at the same tail or head. This emphasizes load balance and       │
│                          │ transit capacity rather than simply accumulating path rewards.                            │
