│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ capped-route-support                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach gives each two-hop route an independent reward, so the combined      │
│                          │ reward for one OD pair can grow with the number of available transit nodes. This version  │
│                          │ instead allocates route rewards proportionally to their attractiveness and scales them    │
│                          │ together only when their total exceeds 0.75 of that pair’s direct-link reward. It uses    │
│                          │ moderate node- and edge-pressure discounts, preserves a small concave component in direct │
│                          │ rewards, and raises the degree-penalty weight from 1.0 to 2.0 to encourage more valid     │
│                          │ samples before repair.                                                                    │
