│ patch_description        │ This design combines a bounded two-hop routing signal with a separate route-diversity     │
│                          │ signal. Rather than rewarding every two-hop route equally, it distributes each OD pair’s  │
│                          │ indirect reward among candidate intermediates, favoring nodes whose traffic profile makes │
│                          │ them plausible relays and discounting heavily loaded relays. It also adds modest positive │
│                          │ interactions between links that provide similar outgoing or incoming service, encouraging │
│                          │ the two degree-constrained choices at a node to cover different traffic patterns. The     │
│                          │ relay-pressure floor is set to 0.85, as suggested; pairwise diversity terms are kept      │
│                          │ modest so they complement rather than overwhelm the direct and indirect demand signals.   │
