│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ capped_route_support                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current two-hop reward is assigned independently across every possible intermediate,  │
│                          │ so its aggregate influence for an OD pair can overwhelm the direct-link signal. Collect   │
│                          │ the candidate two-hop weights per OD pair, then proportionally scale them when their      │
│                          │ total magnitude exceeds 0.75 of that pair’s direct-link reward. This preserves the        │
│                          │ relative preference among intermediates while restraining indirect-route rewards that     │
│                          │ might otherwise distort topology choices.                                                 │
