│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses a direct-demand reward and a fixed-strength reward for every    │
│                          │ eligible two-hop path; across many intermediates, those path rewards can collectively     │
│                          │ overvalue one OD pair. This version keeps the direct reward, but proportionally caps each │
│                          │ OD pair’s total two-hop support at 0.75 of that reward. It allocates the capped support   │
│                          │ among paths using intermediate-node pressure and constituent-link demand, with stronger   │
│                          │ discounts for busy nodes and heavily demanded links. The path strength is 0.50, and the   │
│                          │ degree penalty is raised from 1.0 to 1.35 to encourage more valid samples. Only two-hop   │
│                          │ path terms are generated, keeping the quadratic-term count below the stated limit.        │
