│ patch_description        │ This replaces the path-reward heuristic with a marginal-load model. It estimates how much │
│                          │ traffic each direct link and two-hop path could serve, then discounts paths whose links   │
│                          │ already appear heavily loaded. Quadratic coefficients combine the path’s service benefit  │
│                          │ with a congestion surcharge based on the estimated loads of its two links. This aims to   │
│                          │ reward useful alternate routes without encouraging multiple paths that concentrate        │
│                          │ traffic on the same links.                                                                │
