│ patch_name               │ capped_twohop_support                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ For each positive-demand OD pair, the existing loop can add a reward for every possible   │
│                          │ two-hop route. Together, those alternatives may outweigh the direct-link reward even when │
│                          │ no individual route is compelling. Collect the pair’s two-hop terms and proportionally    │
│                          │ scale them only when their total magnitude exceeds 0.75 of that pair’s direct-link        │
│                          │ reward. This preserves the relative ranking of candidate intermediate nodes while         │
│                          │ limiting aggregate two-hop support. The quadratic term count is unchanged.                │
