│ patch_description        │ Instead of rewarding every possible two-hop route equally, this design gives each         │
│                          │ origin–destination pair a small, demand-weighted portfolio of its most promising          │
│                          │ intermediate nodes. Candidate routes are ranked by estimated edge exposure and            │
│                          │ transit-node pressure, then their rewards are normalized across the portfolio. This       │
│                          │ limits the cumulative incentive to create many overlapping paths while retaining useful   │
│                          │ two-hop structure. Direct-link rewards remain dominant, with a slightly more concave      │
│                          │ demand blend to give moderate-demand links some influence.                                │
