│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ directional_relay_pressure                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Estimate relay pressure from the larger of a node’s incoming and outgoing demand totals,  │
│                          │ rather than their sum. Transit requires both an incoming and an outgoing link, and each   │
│                          │ node has only two of each; a node with a strongly one-sided traffic profile can therefore │
│                          │ be a bottleneck even when its combined incident total looks moderate. Using the larger    │
│                          │ directional total in the existing path discount is a targeted way to discourage           │
│                          │ over-reliance on such relays while leaving direct-link rewards and the number of          │
│                          │ quadratic terms unchanged.                                                                │
