│ patch_name               │ capped-path-support                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current two-hop rewards can accumulate across all possible relays for each OD pair,   │
│                          │ making indirect support dominate the direct-link signal. This version keeps the direct    │
│                          │ reward mostly linear in demand and caps each OD pair’s *aggregate* two-hop reward at 75%  │
│                          │ of its direct reward, scaling its candidate paths proportionally when necessary. Relay    │
│                          │ pressure and component-edge demand still determine the relative ranking of paths. The cap │
│                          │ controls cumulative influence without increasing the quadratic-term count; the degree     │
│                          │ penalty remains evaluator-supplied.                                                       │
