│ patch_name               │ diversity_capacity                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This approach replaces two-hop path rewards with a capacity-diversity proxy. Direct       │
│                          │ traffic still favors useful links, while pairwise penalties discourage a node’s two       │
│                          │ outgoing links from pointing to destinations with similar traffic profiles, or two        │
│                          │ incoming links from coming from sources with similar profiles. Such redundant links are   │
│                          │ less likely to provide diverse routing options. The quadratic terms are sparse—only pairs │
│                          │ sharing a tail or head are considered—and the evaluator remains responsible for degree    │
│                          │ penalties.                                                                                │
