│ patch_name               │ cap_twohop_support                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current two-hop reward is accumulated independently for every intermediate node. For  │
│                          │ an OD pair with many candidate relays, those rewards can collectively outweigh the reward │
│                          │ for building its direct link, giving the QUBO an overly strong incentive to assemble      │
│                          │ paths rather than favor direct service. This edit first computes the candidate path       │
│                          │ rewards for each OD pair, then proportionally caps their total magnitude at 0.75 times    │
│                          │ that pair’s direct-link reward. It retains the relative ranking of relay paths while      │
│                          │ limiting their combined influence. The quadratic term count and degree-penalty handling   │
│                          │ remain unchanged.                                                                         │
