│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cap_twohop_influence                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Limit the aggregate two-hop reward for each origin-destination pair to 75% of that pair’s │
│                          │ direct-link reward. The current code assigns a reward to every feasible intermediate      │
│                          │ node, so many individually modest two-hop terms can collectively dominate the             │
│                          │ direct-service signal. Capping their total magnitude preserves the relative ranking of    │
│                          │ candidate paths while reducing the chance that the QUBO over-favors networks with many    │
│                          │ indirect routes. This follows the supplied recommendation and keeps the number of         │
│                          │ quadratic terms unchanged.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
