│ patch_description        │ This replaces explicit two-hop path rewards with a fractional load-envelope model. It     │
│                          │ estimates each link’s risk from direct demand and the traffic pressure at its endpoints,  │
│                          │ then penalizes selecting pairs of risky links that share a source or destination. The     │
│                          │ sparse pairwise terms discourage concentrated choices without rewarding every possible    │
│                          │ two-hop route equally; direct-demand rewards remain to favor useful links.                │
